# .hankignore: gitignore-style globs, paths relative to the scan root.
# Findings in files matching these globs are suppressed, but ONLY when Hank
# runs with --allow-repo-suppressions: a repo under review must not be able
# to mark itself clean. The report always states how many were suppressed.
# For CI baselines, use --ignore-file with a file outside the scanned tree.

# Hank's own subagent skill describes the very threats it detects, so it
# trips its own rules. Exclude it from a self-scan
# (python3 hank_audit.py . --allow-repo-suppressions). (The intentionally
# vulnerable demo/ is NOT excluded. A root scan still surfaces it, and
# `python3 hank_audit.py demo` exercises every detector.)
skills/hank/**
